Public technical demonstration of AKBASCORE MAM: physical CUT3 memory cartridges written by frozen Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, stored as independent files, addressed from the question by a label-free geometric index and answered from without the source text. Mustafa Akbaş (AkbasCore AI Teknoloji) discovered and developed this memory mechanism (earlier public records: DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23245358, 8 October 2026; DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23257347, 9 October 2026; DOI 10.5281/zenodo.23282902, 10 October 2026); this record is dated 12 October 2026.
Scientific question: Can a frozen language model keep each fact as its own internal key/value state in an independent file on disk, find the right file later from the question alone, and answer from it without being given the source text again?
“The Silicon Hippocampus” names the role of the system: a memory is formed once (WRITE), kept outside the model (SSD) and recalled later (READ). It is a name, not a claim of biological equivalence.
Derived from MAMSH-20261012-053712-0001-C00_FULL_RUN_LOG_payload.json (SHA-256 f85289a8b93a2ad66b1912ea7fdb22a17b4782b12cc0e41abdd81af28a798048). Manifest: run_manifest_MAMSH-20261012-053712-0001-C00.json.
This is a LIVE run of the locked TEST627 demo engine of this runtime. Start-up values were produced by the same engine in this runtime; sealed 627.log / 626.log values are reproduced verbatim, never recomputed.
